2490: /**
2491:  * The other host web servers. When we generate our OWN configuration for one of
2492:  * them, every other one is a latent hazard rather than a spare: they all want
2493:  * port 80/443 and only one can have it.
2494:  *
2495:  * Real incident, 2026-07-25: `apache2` was re-enabled from the source's service
2496:  * list while we generated an nginx config. It could not bind port 80, so it sat
2497:  * `enabled + failed` — quiet today, but first to start after a reboot, where the
2498:  * race decides whether the customer's site or the Apache2 Debian Default Page
2499:  * answers. (The default page is exactly what the customer saw.)
